WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.181 --> 00:00:04.087
- If you're not pursuing
your interests in life,

00:00:04.087 --> 00:00:06.280
you're not realizing who you really are.

00:00:06.280 --> 00:00:08.759
An entrepreneur could
be a business person,

00:00:08.759 --> 00:00:10.462
could be an artist, could be a musician,

00:00:10.462 --> 00:00:13.995
anybody who can have an idea
and turn it into reality.

00:00:13.995 --> 00:00:15.702
Your business can always go away.

00:00:15.702 --> 00:00:17.853
You can never get complacent.

00:00:17.853 --> 00:00:19.928
'Cause I've had it all
taken away from me before.

00:00:19.928 --> 00:00:21.146
I actually was pretty depressed

00:00:21.146 --> 00:00:22.771
when I graduated from college.

00:00:22.771 --> 00:00:24.688
I mean, I was literally
depressed for six months.

00:00:24.688 --> 00:00:26.638
As soon as you are losing steam,

00:00:26.638 --> 00:00:29.032
you've got to bring
people into your business

00:00:29.032 --> 00:00:32.281
that can add a relentless passion to it.

00:00:32.281 --> 00:00:33.704
And the light bulb went off

00:00:33.704 --> 00:00:35.855
and it was literally
like I could see GoPros

00:00:35.855 --> 00:00:38.251
mounted all over the
place and I got chills.

00:00:38.251 --> 00:00:39.267
Why are you laughing?

00:00:39.267 --> 00:00:40.628
(audience laughs)

00:00:40.628 --> 00:00:41.681
My wife is laughing.

00:00:41.681 --> 00:00:42.597
(audience laughs)

00:00:42.597 --> 00:00:44.301
I made the Dean's List.

00:00:44.301 --> 00:00:46.866
- He's an American businessman
and philanthropist.

00:00:46.866 --> 00:00:49.144
He's the founder and CEO of GoPro.

00:00:49.144 --> 00:00:53.282
He has an estimated net
worth of 770 million dollars.

00:00:53.282 --> 00:00:55.036
He's Nick Woodman and here's my take

00:00:55.036 --> 00:00:56.942
on his top ten rules for success.

00:00:56.942 --> 00:00:58.832
Number 10 is my personal favorite

00:00:58.832 --> 00:01:00.377
and make sure to stick around all the way

00:01:00.377 --> 00:01:03.377
to the end for some special bonuses.

00:01:05.475 --> 00:01:08.480
- We all have interests
and passions for a reason.

00:01:08.480 --> 00:01:10.632
It's your inner voice telling you

00:01:10.632 --> 00:01:13.151
what you should be doing with your life.

00:01:13.151 --> 00:01:17.093
If you're not pursuing
your interests in life,

00:01:17.093 --> 00:01:21.200
you're not realizing who you
really are and as a result,

00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:23.907
you're not going to be
as happy as you can be.

00:01:23.907 --> 00:01:27.155
- What does the word
entrepreneur mean to you?

00:01:27.155 --> 00:01:31.322
- When somebody can take
an idea and make it real.

00:01:32.466 --> 00:01:34.906
An entrepreneur could
be a business person,

00:01:34.906 --> 00:01:35.739
could be an artist,

00:01:35.739 --> 00:01:36.602
could be a musician.

00:01:36.602 --> 00:01:40.153
Anybody who can have an idea
and turn it into reality.

00:01:40.153 --> 00:01:42.139
- And how did you do that?

00:01:42.139 --> 00:01:44.037
- I dedicated myself to it.

00:01:44.037 --> 00:01:45.225
When I was 22-years-old,

00:01:45.225 --> 00:01:48.612
I promised myself that
I would work my tail off

00:01:48.612 --> 00:01:51.193
until the age of 30, at a minimum,

00:01:51.193 --> 00:01:53.693
to succeed as an entrepreneur.

00:01:54.720 --> 00:01:57.057
That was extremely important

00:01:57.057 --> 00:01:59.577
because I had a lot of
failure along the way.

00:01:59.577 --> 00:02:01.566
- Right, the first company
you started failed.

00:02:01.566 --> 00:02:03.306
- Yeah, actually and
then there was a company

00:02:03.306 --> 00:02:05.412
that I didn't even start that I failed at.

00:02:05.412 --> 00:02:08.076
So I really had two failures
before I succeeded with GoPro.

00:02:08.076 --> 00:02:11.409
- How do those failures drive you today?

00:02:12.579 --> 00:02:13.412
Does it drive you?
- Well at the time

00:02:13.412 --> 00:02:15.142
they scared me.

00:02:15.142 --> 00:02:16.132
Failure isn't easy.

00:02:16.132 --> 00:02:19.026
It wasn't like I thought,
oh, cool, I failed.

00:02:19.026 --> 00:02:20.595
And success has taught me that one

00:02:20.595 --> 00:02:22.991
of the most important things
an entrepreneur can have

00:02:22.991 --> 00:02:26.453
is perseverance, a dedication,
a willingness to fail,

00:02:26.453 --> 00:02:28.437
pick yourself up again
and give it another shot.

00:02:28.437 --> 00:02:29.430
Because if you don't have that,

00:02:29.430 --> 00:02:31.208
if you don't have that grit,

00:02:31.208 --> 00:02:32.571
you're going to get run over.

00:02:32.571 --> 00:02:34.513
- You started in 2002.

00:02:34.513 --> 00:02:37.279
Let's talk about that
initiation of the dream.

00:02:37.279 --> 00:02:39.091
How did that start and
how'd that come about?

00:02:39.091 --> 00:02:41.725
- I'd started a business before that.

00:02:41.725 --> 00:02:44.966
I raised four million bucks
of other people's money.

00:02:44.966 --> 00:02:48.268
Started a web marketing company.

00:02:48.268 --> 00:02:51.284
Went boom and bust with the
first .com boom and bust.

00:02:51.284 --> 00:02:53.556
I knew I wanted to make
it as an entrepreneur

00:02:53.556 --> 00:02:55.005
and start another
business but I had no idea

00:02:55.005 --> 00:02:56.987
what I wanted to do.

00:02:56.987 --> 00:02:59.904
So, for inspiration, I went surfing

00:03:01.156 --> 00:03:02.643
and I planned a five-month surf trip

00:03:02.643 --> 00:03:05.037
around Australia and Indonesia.

00:03:05.037 --> 00:03:07.184
The inspiration came before I even left.

00:03:07.184 --> 00:03:11.573
I wanted to capture photos
of myself and my friends

00:03:11.573 --> 00:03:12.853
that I was going on the trip with

00:03:12.853 --> 00:03:15.785
while we were surfing out in the water.

00:03:15.785 --> 00:03:18.635
No camera existed that
allowed you to do that.

00:03:18.635 --> 00:03:21.381
And so I set out to
develop this wrist harness

00:03:21.381 --> 00:03:24.098
that I could put a single-use
disposable camera into

00:03:24.098 --> 00:03:25.515
and surf with it.

00:03:27.448 --> 00:03:29.467
I didn't even mean it
to be a business idea,

00:03:29.467 --> 00:03:33.267
I just wanted to document
my experience on this trip.

00:03:33.267 --> 00:03:35.254
As soon as I got it working well,

00:03:35.254 --> 00:03:38.472
the light bulb went off
and I realized, oh my God!

00:03:38.472 --> 00:03:40.231
There must be so many other surfers

00:03:40.231 --> 00:03:42.307
in the world that want
something like this!

00:03:42.307 --> 00:03:44.539
- So you started with
wrist straps, essentially.

00:03:44.539 --> 00:03:47.224
But how do you go from wrist
straps, which are very simple,

00:03:47.224 --> 00:03:49.086
to hardware and to actually
developing a camera?

00:03:49.086 --> 00:03:51.030
- I wanted to use higher quality cameras

00:03:51.030 --> 00:03:53.921
with my wrist strap to
capture higher quality photos

00:03:53.921 --> 00:03:57.477
but every camera that I would
use with the strap surfing,

00:03:57.477 --> 00:03:59.253
I would break the camera.

00:03:59.253 --> 00:04:02.765
Because cameras weren't
designed to be used

00:04:02.765 --> 00:04:05.113
during rigorous activities like surfing.

00:04:05.113 --> 00:04:08.727
What I ended up doing
was I spent two years

00:04:08.727 --> 00:04:10.889
going to trade shows,

00:04:10.889 --> 00:04:12.708
the camera trade shows around the world,

00:04:12.708 --> 00:04:14.473
to look for a camera that was close

00:04:14.473 --> 00:04:17.545
to what I would want to design.

00:04:17.545 --> 00:04:21.712
After a year and a half,
about a year, I found it.

00:04:23.228 --> 00:04:27.449
Got the manufacturer to agree
to make the modifications

00:04:27.449 --> 00:04:29.748
and begin building the cameras for me.

00:04:29.748 --> 00:04:31.024
I actually did the deal without

00:04:31.024 --> 00:04:33.241
ever meeting the actual company.

00:04:33.241 --> 00:04:34.204
It was all e-mail.

00:04:34.204 --> 00:04:36.052
I had one phone call where we could

00:04:36.052 --> 00:04:37.083
barely understand each other

00:04:37.083 --> 00:04:38.314
because of language barriers.

00:04:38.314 --> 00:04:39.297
- Were they Chinese?

00:04:39.297 --> 00:04:40.130
- They're in Shenzhen.

00:04:40.130 --> 00:04:43.213
I wired my $5,000 for the tool to be,

00:04:45.476 --> 00:04:47.373
the mold to be made

00:04:47.373 --> 00:04:50.953
because it was actually
cheaper just to wire five grand

00:04:50.953 --> 00:04:52.391
than to fly over there, meet them,

00:04:52.391 --> 00:04:54.065
have a business trip and I just figured,

00:04:54.065 --> 00:04:55.382
okay, we'll just go for it,

00:04:55.382 --> 00:04:58.251
and they ended up being legitimate.

00:04:58.251 --> 00:04:59.733
We were profitable from day one

00:04:59.733 --> 00:05:02.198
because it was just me, one employee.

00:05:02.198 --> 00:05:03.674
We just had no overhead

00:05:03.674 --> 00:05:06.758
and rolled one good production run

00:05:06.758 --> 00:05:09.222
into another and slowly scaled it.

00:05:09.222 --> 00:05:12.253
The GoPro that everybody knows today

00:05:12.253 --> 00:05:15.420
has been built on $265,000 of capital.

00:05:16.949 --> 00:05:18.180
The Hero4 Session

00:05:18.180 --> 00:05:22.022
is the first GoPro we've ever released

00:05:22.022 --> 00:05:24.897
that didn't immediately take off.

00:05:24.897 --> 00:05:26.350
It wasn't just that we're selling

00:05:26.350 --> 00:05:30.914
against the strength of
HERO4 Black and Silver,

00:05:30.914 --> 00:05:34.652
we also gaffed it and priced it wrong.

00:05:34.652 --> 00:05:36.618
What I'm proud of is
that when we recognized

00:05:36.618 --> 00:05:39.126
that we mis-priced GoPro,

00:05:39.126 --> 00:05:41.965
and that it wasn't in the
interest of the customer

00:05:41.965 --> 00:05:44.099
and the customer just
wasn't grooving on it,

00:05:44.099 --> 00:05:44.932
we changed it.

00:05:44.932 --> 00:05:47.386
It's not the last time we're
going to make moves like that,

00:05:47.386 --> 00:05:51.659
a radical that are in favor
of the customer's experience

00:05:51.659 --> 00:05:53.507
but if we can keep doing that,

00:05:53.507 --> 00:05:56.009
we can keep differentiating
ourselves from how

00:05:56.009 --> 00:05:57.855
a lot of other businesses operate

00:05:57.855 --> 00:05:59.855
and that differentiation

00:06:00.929 --> 00:06:03.246
is part of what makes
this company so special.

00:06:03.246 --> 00:06:05.589
- How do you keep GoPro,

00:06:05.589 --> 00:06:07.027
what you're famous for,

00:06:07.027 --> 00:06:11.085
how do you keep it the best of the bunch?

00:06:11.085 --> 00:06:13.659
- Well, having failed a couple times,

00:06:13.659 --> 00:06:17.826
I recognize that your
business can always go away.

00:06:19.433 --> 00:06:21.526
You can never get complacent

00:06:21.526 --> 00:06:24.762
'cause I've had it all
taken away from me before.

00:06:24.762 --> 00:06:26.949
It's important to wake up every morning

00:06:26.949 --> 00:06:30.625
a little bit scared
that that might happen.

00:06:30.625 --> 00:06:33.433
Never think that you've finally made it

00:06:33.433 --> 00:06:34.539
- Does Shuame scare you?

00:06:34.539 --> 00:06:35.385
Does Apple scare you?

00:06:35.385 --> 00:06:36.242
- No, no, no.

00:06:36.242 --> 00:06:38.087
Actually, competition
is a really good thing

00:06:38.087 --> 00:06:40.883
because, yeah, of course
they scare you a little bit.

00:06:40.883 --> 00:06:42.776
That's a good thing because it drives you.

00:06:42.776 --> 00:06:44.700
It motivates you to put
more into your work,

00:06:44.700 --> 00:06:47.614
to stay running and stay running hard

00:06:47.614 --> 00:06:49.793
and that's something that we,

00:06:49.793 --> 00:06:51.996
is alive and well at our culture,

00:06:51.996 --> 00:06:53.283
and I think it's also important

00:06:53.283 --> 00:06:56.096
to never let yourself
stop being a start-up.

00:06:56.096 --> 00:06:58.277
Stop trying to re-invent yourself.

00:06:58.277 --> 00:06:59.797
- You're getting new video all the time.

00:06:59.797 --> 00:07:01.855
- All the time.

00:07:01.855 --> 00:07:05.064
This is actually a video of a firefighter

00:07:05.064 --> 00:07:08.318
rescuing and resuscitating a kitten.

00:07:08.318 --> 00:07:09.151
- Yeah.

00:07:09.151 --> 00:07:10.293
- And a video like that

00:07:10.293 --> 00:07:12.690
would very easily go viral
all around the world.

00:07:12.690 --> 00:07:13.523
I mean--

00:07:13.523 --> 00:07:15.056
- Oh my, God, yeah.

00:07:15.056 --> 00:07:17.787
- That's essentially a
commercial for GoPro.

00:07:17.787 --> 00:07:19.907
- Essentially a commercial for GoPro.

00:07:19.907 --> 00:07:20.966
(kitten meowing)

00:07:20.966 --> 00:07:22.513
It's a marketer's dream

00:07:22.513 --> 00:07:25.531
and it's all based off
of authenticity, right?

00:07:25.531 --> 00:07:28.337
It's our customers
doing interesting things

00:07:28.337 --> 00:07:30.904
around the world and they're so stoked

00:07:30.904 --> 00:07:33.618
that they're able to finally self-document

00:07:33.618 --> 00:07:34.896
these things that they like to do

00:07:34.896 --> 00:07:36.172
and share it with people.

00:07:36.172 --> 00:07:38.483
They're so stoked at how
good they look in the video

00:07:38.483 --> 00:07:39.633
that when they share the video,

00:07:39.633 --> 00:07:40.923
they often give us credit.

00:07:40.923 --> 00:07:42.075
My GoPro ski trip.

00:07:42.075 --> 00:07:44.417
My GoPro day at the park with my kids.

00:07:44.417 --> 00:07:46.225
- You're the only CO that
I've ever interviewed

00:07:46.225 --> 00:07:47.414
who's used the word stoked.

00:07:47.414 --> 00:07:48.911
- Like five million times.

00:07:48.911 --> 00:07:50.075
- Five million times, yes.

00:07:50.075 --> 00:07:54.242
- Well, you know, you've got
to stay true to who you are

00:07:55.352 --> 00:07:58.685
and I recognize that my approach to life

00:08:00.289 --> 00:08:03.083
and now our company's approach to life

00:08:03.083 --> 00:08:05.171
is what has made GoPro what it is

00:08:05.171 --> 00:08:07.022
and so there's no reason to change that.

00:08:07.022 --> 00:08:08.135
Everybody around me,

00:08:08.135 --> 00:08:10.149
their parents were lawyers

00:08:10.149 --> 00:08:13.767
or investment bankers or entrepreneurs.

00:08:13.767 --> 00:08:15.741
They were all involved in business.

00:08:15.741 --> 00:08:18.198
That actually didn't seem very
much fun to me growing up.

00:08:18.198 --> 00:08:21.569
I thought that being an
adult's kind of a drag.

00:08:21.569 --> 00:08:22.799
I actually was pretty depressed

00:08:22.799 --> 00:08:24.477
when I graduated from college.

00:08:24.477 --> 00:08:26.575
I mean, I was literally
depressed for like six months.

00:08:26.575 --> 00:08:29.618
I woke up at one o'clock in the afternoon

00:08:29.618 --> 00:08:31.299
and laid on a couch and
looked up at the ceiling

00:08:31.299 --> 00:08:33.479
and was just like, dude,
what am I going to do?

00:08:33.479 --> 00:08:38.212
So, with no inspiration, I
just decided, you know what?

00:08:38.212 --> 00:08:40.251
The only thing I can
think of to do right now

00:08:40.251 --> 00:08:43.500
that's going to make me
happy is if I go surfing.

00:08:43.500 --> 00:08:44.829
So I planned a five month trip

00:08:44.829 --> 00:08:46.309
around Australia and Indonesia

00:08:46.309 --> 00:08:49.432
living out of a back pack
and a van at the time.

00:08:49.432 --> 00:08:52.270
If I didn't follow my passion for surfing,

00:08:52.270 --> 00:08:56.230
I would have never had the idea for GoPro.

00:08:56.230 --> 00:08:58.730
You have got to be relentless.

00:08:59.638 --> 00:09:03.555
One of the things that's
really benefited GoPro

00:09:04.486 --> 00:09:06.569
is a healthy dose of fear

00:09:07.403 --> 00:09:10.070
that you're going to get
taken out by somebody

00:09:10.070 --> 00:09:14.095
and a healthy enthusiasm
for all of your great ideas

00:09:14.095 --> 00:09:18.262
and being impatient as hell
to bring them to reality.

00:09:21.550 --> 00:09:24.246
You know, having failed in business before

00:09:24.246 --> 00:09:26.830
scared the hell out of me.

00:09:26.830 --> 00:09:28.893
You know, I still wake up scared

00:09:28.893 --> 00:09:30.245
that it's all going to go away.

00:09:30.245 --> 00:09:31.078
- Right.

00:09:31.078 --> 00:09:33.332
- Less scared than I used to be.

00:09:33.332 --> 00:09:35.302
But it happens.

00:09:35.302 --> 00:09:38.954
You can never say, ahh, we made it,

00:09:38.954 --> 00:09:41.748
'cause that's when you get
hit by the competitive truck.

00:09:41.748 --> 00:09:42.733
- Or a surf board.

00:09:42.733 --> 00:09:44.768
- Or a surf board.

00:09:44.768 --> 00:09:47.221
You have to stay scared

00:09:47.221 --> 00:09:51.136
and you also have to really,
really, really be relentless.

00:09:51.136 --> 00:09:54.626
I always think about what
is the other company doing?

00:09:54.626 --> 00:09:56.925
The other guy or gal,

00:09:56.925 --> 00:09:58.034
what is their mindset

00:09:58.034 --> 00:10:01.277
and how can we be more
aggressive than them?

00:10:01.277 --> 00:10:05.595
How can we have a more aggressive roadmap,

00:10:05.595 --> 00:10:07.153
development time line

00:10:07.153 --> 00:10:11.003
to where we just absolutely
out-pace the competition?

00:10:11.003 --> 00:10:12.485
Just wear them into the ground.

00:10:12.485 --> 00:10:13.318
- Sure.

00:10:13.318 --> 00:10:14.485
- I think that

00:10:16.740 --> 00:10:20.116
that's been one of the
secrets to our success.

00:10:20.116 --> 00:10:23.149
If you look at our development

00:10:23.149 --> 00:10:25.049
and product release history,

00:10:25.049 --> 00:10:27.719
from the HERO to the HERO2 to the HERO3

00:10:27.719 --> 00:10:30.264
to the HERO3+ to the HERO4,

00:10:30.264 --> 00:10:34.913
we've launched five new
cameras in the last 11 months.

00:10:34.913 --> 00:10:37.992
We've made significant
advancements in our software,

00:10:37.992 --> 00:10:41.566
all the while expanding
our global marketing,

00:10:41.566 --> 00:10:45.518
growing into more than
40,000 retail stores

00:10:45.518 --> 00:10:47.979
with our in-store retail merchandisers

00:10:47.979 --> 00:10:50.563
in every single store.

00:10:50.563 --> 00:10:52.581
Once we have those in
store, that's not enough.

00:10:52.581 --> 00:10:53.859
Now, we need to grow footprints.

00:10:53.859 --> 00:10:56.273
So we grow from two linear feet

00:10:56.273 --> 00:10:59.190
of retail merchandising shelf space

00:11:00.131 --> 00:11:04.318
to now 12 feet in big
stores like Best Buy.

00:11:04.318 --> 00:11:06.042
Even our smaller format stores

00:11:06.042 --> 00:11:10.209
are going from two to five
to some eight feet of linear.

00:11:12.898 --> 00:11:15.080
You can never be done.

00:11:15.080 --> 00:11:16.234
- So you've got to be relentless.

00:11:16.234 --> 00:11:17.836
- You have to be relentless

00:11:17.836 --> 00:11:20.011
and as soon as you are losing steam,

00:11:20.011 --> 00:11:22.282
you've got to bring
people into your business

00:11:22.282 --> 00:11:25.597
that can add a relentless passion to it.

00:11:25.597 --> 00:11:28.184
If you don't feel like you're relentless,

00:11:28.184 --> 00:11:29.457
chances are that you're competing

00:11:29.457 --> 00:11:31.457
against somebody who is.

00:11:32.780 --> 00:11:34.353
It's a race.

00:11:34.353 --> 00:11:36.770
As long as you can bootstrap,

00:11:40.555 --> 00:11:44.388
not at the sacrifice of
competitive advantage,

00:11:46.767 --> 00:11:48.448
meaning not leaving yourself open,

00:11:48.448 --> 00:11:50.837
not moving so slowly
that you leave yourself

00:11:50.837 --> 00:11:53.935
to be eaten alive by your competitors.

00:11:53.935 --> 00:11:56.492
Bootstrapping is a really powerful thing

00:11:56.492 --> 00:12:00.659
because it allows you to be
totally devoted to your vision

00:12:04.051 --> 00:12:08.578
and not have to deal with
the pressures of investors

00:12:08.578 --> 00:12:12.440
to maybe realize milestones
and unrealistic timelines.

00:12:12.440 --> 00:12:13.273
- Sure.

00:12:14.245 --> 00:12:16.269
- Everybody has an idea over time

00:12:16.269 --> 00:12:19.015
of what the business should be.

00:12:19.015 --> 00:12:22.718
When the business is going
well, people leave you alone.

00:12:22.718 --> 00:12:25.792
But I think maybe during
the formative period,

00:12:25.792 --> 00:12:28.959
too many opinions could be disruptive.

00:12:32.045 --> 00:12:34.337
I know it really helped GoPro

00:12:34.337 --> 00:12:37.782
that we didn't have to
answer to anybody for years.

00:12:37.782 --> 00:12:40.683
I think an example is when we,

00:12:40.683 --> 00:12:44.013
as soon as we could afford
it, we bought a race car.

00:12:44.013 --> 00:12:48.528
We went racing up at
Sonoma Raceway in Sonoma

00:12:48.528 --> 00:12:50.171
and I learned how to drive a race car

00:12:50.171 --> 00:12:54.628
and I became our chief R&amp;D
developer for motor sport.

00:12:54.628 --> 00:12:55.461
- When you're the founder,

00:12:55.461 --> 00:12:56.355
you can do whatever you want to do.

00:12:56.355 --> 00:12:59.067
- Yeah, but if we'd had
investors at that point,

00:12:59.067 --> 00:13:00.586
they might have questioned, you know,

00:13:00.586 --> 00:13:04.816
is this really a great
use of company proceeds?

00:13:04.816 --> 00:13:05.803
In the end,

00:13:05.803 --> 00:13:08.142
it led to one of the biggest ideas

00:13:08.142 --> 00:13:09.495
that we ever had at GoPro,

00:13:09.495 --> 00:13:12.005
which was to get the
camera off of the wrist

00:13:12.005 --> 00:13:14.185
and make mounting accessories

00:13:14.185 --> 00:13:16.375
so that you could use the camera,

00:13:16.375 --> 00:13:19.941
mount the camera in any way imaginable.

00:13:19.941 --> 00:13:22.395
The way that that happened was

00:13:22.395 --> 00:13:23.390
I was in racing school

00:13:23.390 --> 00:13:25.726
and they wanted to charge
me a bunch of money

00:13:25.726 --> 00:13:26.796
to put a camera on the car.

00:13:26.796 --> 00:13:27.954
And I thought, that's crazy.

00:13:27.954 --> 00:13:29.922
I've got my wrist camera in my trunk

00:13:29.922 --> 00:13:31.397
of my street car.

00:13:31.397 --> 00:13:32.384
I went and got it,

00:13:32.384 --> 00:13:34.235
strapped it to the roll bar,

00:13:34.235 --> 00:13:35.712
and the light bulb went off.

00:13:35.712 --> 00:13:37.928
It was literally like I could see GoPro's

00:13:37.928 --> 00:13:39.123
mounted all over the place.

00:13:39.123 --> 00:13:40.206
I got chills.

00:13:41.057 --> 00:13:41.923
Until then,

00:13:41.923 --> 00:13:44.970
we had been a little wrist
camera company plodding along.

00:13:44.970 --> 00:13:47.697
Then that was a major hockey stick moment

00:13:47.697 --> 00:13:49.664
for the company that was totally inspired

00:13:49.664 --> 00:13:50.976
by climbing into a race car,

00:13:50.976 --> 00:13:53.209
which is not what a board of directors

00:13:53.209 --> 00:13:54.897
would normally think was a great idea.

00:13:54.897 --> 00:13:57.871
I had a deal with my parents that

00:13:57.871 --> 00:13:59.538
I got into Berkeley.

00:14:01.489 --> 00:14:03.572
But I didn't get in here.

00:14:05.002 --> 00:14:06.909
I was terrified of going to Berkeley

00:14:06.909 --> 00:14:08.385
'cause it was so close to home.

00:14:08.385 --> 00:14:10.110
(laughing)

00:14:10.110 --> 00:14:13.910
My parents said, "You know what we said

00:14:13.910 --> 00:14:16.487
"about you being able to pick
where you can go to school?"

00:14:16.487 --> 00:14:17.594
"Yeah."

00:14:17.594 --> 00:14:20.110
"As soon as you got into
Berkeley that choice went away.

00:14:20.110 --> 00:14:21.551
"You're going there."

00:14:21.551 --> 00:14:22.457
And I made a deal with them

00:14:22.457 --> 00:14:24.514
that if I could get into UC San Diego,

00:14:24.514 --> 00:14:25.666
would they let me go here?

00:14:25.666 --> 00:14:27.364
This is where I wanted to go

00:14:27.364 --> 00:14:29.628
and my motivation was it
was the best education

00:14:29.628 --> 00:14:31.307
combined with the best surf.

00:14:31.307 --> 00:14:32.897
I mean, just,

00:14:32.897 --> 00:14:34.805
just being honest.

00:14:34.805 --> 00:14:39.803
(laughing)
(audience applauding)

00:14:39.803 --> 00:14:43.136
I wrote a very earnest letter of appeal.

00:14:44.324 --> 00:14:45.991
Thank God, I got in!

00:14:47.649 --> 00:14:51.996
The rest is the history that
we're continuing to write.

00:14:51.996 --> 00:14:54.087
- What was the case that you made?

00:14:54.087 --> 00:14:55.565
Do you remember?

00:14:55.565 --> 00:14:56.632
- Yeah.

00:14:56.632 --> 00:15:00.132
I promised that I would really buckle down

00:15:02.594 --> 00:15:04.232
and put my head down.
(wife laughs)

00:15:04.232 --> 00:15:05.589
Why are you laughing?

00:15:05.589 --> 00:15:06.865
(audience laughs)

00:15:06.865 --> 00:15:08.882
My wife is laughing.

00:15:08.882 --> 00:15:11.167
I made the Dean's list.

00:15:11.167 --> 00:15:13.703
(audience laughs)

00:15:13.703 --> 00:15:16.078
In my freshman year, I think I made it.

00:15:16.078 --> 00:15:18.627
I think I made it once or twice,

00:15:18.627 --> 00:15:21.497
then kind of fell from there.

00:15:21.497 --> 00:15:23.755
I promised to really devote myself

00:15:23.755 --> 00:15:27.005
and make the most out of the education.

00:15:28.682 --> 00:15:29.916
That I wasn't coming to party.

00:15:29.916 --> 00:15:33.416
That I wasn't coming just to screw around.

00:15:34.551 --> 00:15:37.259
That if UC San Diego would
give me the opportunity,

00:15:37.259 --> 00:15:41.426
I would really make something
of myself at the school.

00:15:42.709 --> 00:15:45.376
Thanks for taking a flyer on me.

00:15:47.122 --> 00:15:50.116
The lesson there just is never give up.

00:15:50.116 --> 00:15:51.145
Never give up.

00:15:51.145 --> 00:15:52.051
'Cause if I went to Berkeley,

00:15:52.051 --> 00:15:54.156
I don't think I would have had the...

00:15:54.156 --> 00:15:56.164
That life is a winding path.

00:15:56.164 --> 00:15:58.792
I just don't think I
would have had the same

00:15:58.792 --> 00:16:02.186
interests and inspiration
there that led me, ultimately,

00:16:02.186 --> 00:16:03.936
to my idea for GoPro.

00:16:06.207 --> 00:16:07.329
- Thank you guys so much for watching!

00:16:07.329 --> 00:16:08.191
I hope you enjoyed.

00:16:08.191 --> 00:16:12.507
I made this video because
grnhy asked me to.

00:16:12.507 --> 00:16:13.695
So if there's a famous entrepreneur

00:16:13.695 --> 00:16:15.913
you want me to profile next,
leave in the comments below

00:16:15.913 --> 00:16:17.316
and I'll see what I can do.

00:16:17.316 --> 00:16:19.407
I'd also love to know
which of the top 10 rules

00:16:19.407 --> 00:16:21.545
had the biggest impact on you and why.

00:16:21.545 --> 00:16:23.804
Leave them in the comments and
I will join the discussion.

00:16:23.804 --> 00:16:25.285
Thank you so much for watching.

00:16:25.285 --> 00:16:28.785
Continue to believe and I'll see you soon.

00:16:33.827 --> 00:16:35.548
- A secret to GoPro's success,

00:16:35.548 --> 00:16:39.495
people would wonder how did
you cash flow the business?

00:16:39.495 --> 00:16:42.718
We learned early on that our
international distributors

00:16:42.718 --> 00:16:45.678
would pay FOB Hong Kong, right?

00:16:45.678 --> 00:16:49.206
They would pay when we would
ship to them from Hong Kong.

00:16:49.206 --> 00:16:51.135
We would, in the day, get paid

00:16:51.135 --> 00:16:53.443
by our international customers

00:16:53.443 --> 00:16:56.761
before we even owed the factory the money.

00:16:56.761 --> 00:16:59.120
We went against the grain,

00:16:59.120 --> 00:17:01.666
and we built our
international business first

00:17:01.666 --> 00:17:03.880
because they would pay up front.

00:17:03.880 --> 00:17:06.220
We used the international revenue

00:17:06.220 --> 00:17:08.819
to build the domestic
business which is the inverse

00:17:08.819 --> 00:17:13.311
of what traditional business
logic would tell you,

00:17:13.311 --> 00:17:15.782
which is build your domestic brand first

00:17:15.782 --> 00:17:17.139
and then take it overseas.

00:17:17.139 --> 00:17:19.360
I don't know that that really
works this day and age.

00:17:19.360 --> 00:17:22.903
You'd pretty much have
to build globally quickly

00:17:22.903 --> 00:17:25.214
or else somebody else'll do it for you.

00:17:25.214 --> 00:17:26.732
Everything you need to succeed in life

00:17:26.732 --> 00:17:29.067
is already out there.

00:17:29.067 --> 00:17:31.184
You don't need a ton of money

00:17:31.184 --> 00:17:34.517
and just go be scrappy and be dedicated,

00:17:36.713 --> 00:17:39.463
and you can build your own GoPro.

